Here is a complete package.json for a small Node-only project:
```json
{
  "name": "repro-demo",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node main.js"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=22.13.0"
  },
  "dependencies": {}
}
```
start says how to launch; engines documents the required Node version. >= means this version or newer. The empty dependencies object is accurate because this greeting uses only Node's built-in features. engines is normally a compatibility declaration, not an automatic installation of the runtime.

